  "oracle_rules": [
    "Independently parse original finite numeric strings to exact integer/rational numbers; time offset seconds*1e9 must be integral and source times nondecreasing within [0,86400).",
    "Compute raw_price/(scale*tick) as a single exact rational expression; reject off-grid configured prices, never round an intermediate display price.",
    "Use independent integer datetime epoch arithmetic, never float timestamp or production converter/calendar helper.",
    "Initial visible message is validated but represented by RESET then BID/ASK SNAPSHOT only. Two-row valid cases then emit exactly one BID TRADE of quantity1 at the original raw bid; independently reconstruct post-message book.",
    "Zero-size dummy levels skip their prices; negative dummy price is not active liquidity. Message-only negative case is an initial submission below the visible bid: an unseen lower-level addition can leave the one-level paired snapshot unchanged, but its off-configured-tick raw price must still be rejected.",
    "Require exact canonical rows including event type, time/sequence/side/price/quantity, helper boundary raw strings, strict dictionary reconstruction/certificate, causal_trade_events=1 and no window reconciliation in two-row positive cases. A book-only price fix that leaves message conversion rounded must fail (it can turn a TRADE into reconciliation CANCEL)."
  ],
